    },
    "message": "fix(install): stop relying on script scope in the Windows installer\n\nThe published Windows command runs install.ps1 as a scriptblock\n(irm ... | iex), and under that form a function's $script: writes are not\nvisible to the rest of the script. Resolve-Release set $script:FccWheelUrl and\nfriends, so the real install called Invoke-RestMethod with an empty URI and\ndied on 'Invalid URI: The hostname could not be parsed'.\n\nNothing caught it: the file parses, and running it with -File works, because\nthat form does give functions the script scope. Only the published invocation\nfails.\n\nResolve-Release now returns the resolved release and callers take it as a\nparameter, so the flow no longer depends on scope semantics that vary by how\nthe script is invoked. Adds a test asserting that.",
